<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service — UPos" description="Terms governing access to and use of the UPos retail software service.">
  <section class="legal-hero compact"><div class="shell"><p class="kicker"><span></span> Legal</p><h1>Terms of Service</h1><p>Last updated: {company.lastUpdated}</p></div></section>
  <article class="legal-copy shell"><p>These Terms of Service (“Terms”) form an agreement between you and <strong>{company.legalName}</strong> (“UPos”, “we”, “us”) for your access to and use of the UPos software and related services (the “Service”). By creating an account, starting a trial, or purchasing a subscription, you agree to these Terms.</p><h2>1. The Service</h2><p>UPos provides point-of-sale, inventory, shift, reporting and related retail-management tools. Specific features and usage limits depend on your plan. We may improve the Service over time, provided that we do not materially reduce the core functionality of a paid plan during its current term.</p><h2>2. Eligibility and accounts</h2><p>You must be legally able to enter a binding contract and use the Service for lawful business purposes. You are responsible for accurate account information, authorized users, protecting credentials and all activity under your account. Notify us promptly of suspected unauthorized access.</p><h2>3. Trials, fees and renewal</h2><p>Trials last 14 days unless stated otherwise. A trial does not convert to a paid subscription unless you complete checkout. Paid subscriptions renew automatically monthly or annually at the price shown at checkout until cancelled. Prices are displayed in USD; applicable taxes are calculated at checkout. We will provide reasonable notice of price changes, which apply from a future renewal.</p><h2>4. Payment provider</h2><p><strong>Our order process is conducted by our online reseller Paddle.com. Paddle.com is the Merchant of Record for all our orders. Paddle provides all customer service inquiries and handles returns.</strong> At checkout, you also agree to Paddle’s applicable buyer terms. Paddle handles payment processing, sales tax and invoices.</p><h2>5. Cancellation and refunds</h2><p>You may cancel before the next renewal through the buyer portal or by contacting us. Access continues until the end of the paid term. Refund eligibility is described in our <a href="/refund-policy/">Refund Policy</a>, which forms part of these Terms.</p><h2>6. Acceptable use</h2><p>You may not use the Service unlawfully; attempt to bypass security or access controls; interfere with the Service; upload malicious code; copy, resell or reverse engineer the Service except where law permits; or use it to infringe another person’s rights. We may suspend access where reasonably necessary to protect customers or the Service.</p><h2>7. Your data</h2><p>You retain ownership of data you submit. You grant us permission to process it only as needed to provide, secure and improve the Service, comply with law and fulfill our obligations. Our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains our practices.</p><h2>8. Availability and support</h2><p>We aim to provide a reliable Service but do not guarantee uninterrupted availability. Planned maintenance, internet failures and events beyond reasonable control may affect access. Support is available at <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>, typically within 2 business days.</p><h2>9. Intellectual property</h2><p>The Service, brand, design and underlying technology are owned by or licensed to UPos. These Terms grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the Service during your trial or paid subscription.</p><h2>10. Warranties and liability</h2><p>To the extent permitted by law, the Service is provided “as is”. We do not exclude rights or liabilities that cannot legally be excluded. Our aggregate liability arising from the Service will not exceed the fees you paid for the Service in the 12 months before the event giving rise to the claim. We are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, lost profits or lost data where exclusion is permitted.</p><h2>11. Termination</h2><p>You may stop using the Service at any time. We may terminate or suspend access for a material breach, unlawful use, non-payment or a security risk, normally after giving reasonable notice and an opportunity to remedy where appropriate.</p><h2>12. Changes and governing law</h2><p>We may update these Terms and will post the revised date. Material changes will be communicated reasonably in advance. These Terms are governed by the laws of Georgia, and its courts have jurisdiction, subject to any mandatory consumer protections that apply to you.</p><h2>13. Contact</h2><p>{company.legalName}<br/>{company.address}<br/><a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a><br/>{company.phone}</p></article>
</BaseLayout>
